Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"48e7b350-a1b4-8344-879e-9f89a9b51480"],

Cell["\<\
1. Visualise the sqrt(2) corner violation: Compare \"Cartesian Box\" vs \
\"Polar Disk\" at RF Limit = 85 Hz in Lab 6A. Look at points landing outside \
the red circle on the 2D (ux, uy) plot under Box bounds.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"edbc9916-e10e-3048-b270-99590bcd0ae9"],

Cell["\<\
2. Plateau formation: Switch Constraint Mode to \"Disk + L1 + TV\" and \
inspect how Total Variation shrinks cleanly into stepped DANTE-like constant \
plateaus.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ff74a6ce-cf7c-5642-a5d0-69f7be86db4c"],

Cell["\<\
3. Slew-rate feasibility: Tightly lower Slew Bound toward 8000 Hz/s and watch \
step changes flatten cleanly with zero constraint violation.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9185b9a1-483f-2747-ac26-126318edc81e"],

Cell["\<\
4. Hardware Resampling: In Lab 6B, switch Bruker Export from Resample -> \
Automatic (24 points) to Resample -> 12 and check the ##NPOINTS= header \
update.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"552dd430-af5c-e847-8146-52db04394253"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3c882a60-9010-1542-8759-eeb5447df6ef"],

Cell["\<\
Polar disk bounds enforce physical RF nutation ceilings strictly; FISTA \
paired with Condat 1D TV and multi-block ADMM solves slew-limited and \
L1/TV-regularised problems cleanly while preserving export fidelity across \
Bruker, SIMPSON, and CSV formats.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e520f5ea-e1c1-3b44-80ed-9f33a6a31168"],

